## Fixed 2026-09-05 (commit aebe974, Gerrit 235)

Safari resolves the click of a pointer-captured drag to the element under the pointer at release — the header, not the grip — so the header's own click handler opened the field tray after every resize. The grip now marks its header for the gesture (`data-resized`) and the header click is inert until the next press anywhere; a plain click still opens the tray. The drag also paints header and cells on every move (see Issue #160), so it tracks the pointer instead of lurching. Tests: `test/column-fit.test.mjs` (a 6px drag leaves `#tray-back` closed, a plain click opens it); `test/ui-contract.test.mjs` pins the guard.

