## Fixed — 2026-09-02 (Gerrit 187)

The grid cell was a read-only chip whose tooltip said "edit on the record page" — the replay shows eleven clicks on it. The cell now holds the same two date controls the record page uses (typed dates and the calendar at either end), compact, with the dash travelling with the end so a column too narrow for both wraps as "start / – end" rather than clipping the end. A half-written range still commits nothing until both ends read as dates. Gate: `test/daterange-browser.test.mjs` opens the table, finds two date controls in the Window cell, edits the end, and reads the committed range back from the engine.



Merged 2026-09-02 21:07 PT as bd45353 (Gerrit 187, patchset 3 — the first gate caught the dash grouping widening the range on a one-column record page; it is now scoped to grid cells).

Reproduced on gerrit/main cc3b8d9 (v0.4.54) through the engine verbs alone, no build call:

```js
w.createSpace({name:'S'}); w.createTable({space:'S',name:'A'}); w.createTable({space:'S',name:'T'});
w.addField('A',{name:'K',type:'select',config:{options:[{name:'Credit card'}]}});
w.addRelation('T',{name:'A',targetDb:'A'});
w.addField('T',{name:'L',type:'lookup',config:{relationField:'A',targetField:'K'}});
w.createEntity('A',{Name:'a',K:'Credit card'});
const t = w.createEntity('T',{Name:'t',A:'a'});
w.readEntity(t.id).fields.L   // "credit-card"
w.readEntity(t.id).raw.L      // "credit-card"
w.query('T',{}).items[0]      // L: "credit-card"
```

The display value of the lookup (readEntity `fields`, the query row) is the option's stored id, the slug, where the select column on table A shows "Credit card". An option whose name is already a slug ("x") hides the bug, which is why it went unseen.

Good looks like Airtable and Notion: a lookup of a single select shows the same chip, with the same name and colour, as the source column.

Fix shape: resolve the lookup's display through the target field's costume (option name and colour for select and multiselect, state name for workflow), the way the source column displays itself; keep raw as the id if raw is meant to be stored values. Test: a lookup of a select whose option name differs from its slug.

Filed by the build-verb session (Feature #253), 2026-10-02, v0.4.54, commit cc3b8d9.

Fixed by Gerrit change 590 (commit c87b9b1, fast-forwarded onto gerrit/main after v0.4.65), 2026-10-05, session reverent-cray-353456. #displayValue gains a lookup case: a lookup of a select, multiselect or workflow dresses each value through the far field, so it reads the option or state name; raw keeps the ids. Gate: test/lookup-option-name.test.mjs (single and many lookups; readEntity, query rows, select, where, weave_get_entity). Option colour on the computed cell is not in this change. Fixed in: the next release (unreleased at filing).

